{:id :EACL-FORMAL-005
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :dafny
 :seed-or-trace "portable-cursor/expires-at-boundary"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :stale-reuse
 :affected-versions ["current worktree at discovery"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "Portable cursor decoding ignored the injected clock used by deterministic CLJ/CLJS tests and considered a token valid while now equaled expires-at. Datomic's encrypted cursor already rejects at equality, so identical expiry metadata had different validity across backends."
 :fix
 "The portable cursor now uses the caller-supplied deterministic clock when present and rejects when now is greater than or equal to expires-at, matching Datomic and the Dafny cursor predicate."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.secure-format-test/portable-cursor-expiry-boundary-test (CLJ and CLJS)"
  "formal/dafny/TemporalSafety.dfy ValidateCursor expiry branch"]}
